# AI Agent Workflows

## Bootstrap (every task)

Execute `docs/ai_bootstrap_prompt.md` before implementation:

1. Read docs 1–5 in order
2. Summarize business, architecture, branch, inventory, UI, sprint context
3. Identify affected modules/services/repositories/policies/tests
4. Run Sprint Consistency Check (Sprints 10–12)
5. Produce scoped implementation plan — **wait for approval** before coding
6. Implement in phases; run quality gates; deliver honest summary

## Context-Mode Workflow

Use when processing large outputs (test runs, logs, diffs, migrations, route lists):

- Prefer `ctx_execute` / `ctx_execute_file` over dumping raw terminal output into context
- Use `ctx_search` for previously indexed project knowledge before re-reading large files
- Index durable docs (`docs/architecture_rules.md`, module folders) with `ctx_index` when starting long sessions
- Trigger on: test output, build logs, git history, API responses, security audits

## Claude-Mem Workflow

Use for cross-session continuity:

- `mem-search` before re-solving problems ("did we already fix branch leakage in X?")
- Reference `docs/sprint_history.md` for permanent decisions; mem-search for session-specific fixes
- After significant architectural decisions, capture rationale aligned with sprint history numbering
- Do not contradict locked sprint decisions (BranchContext, ledger inventory, layering)

## Frontend-Design Workflow

When building or modernizing UI pages/components:

- Read `docs/ui_design_system.md` and inspect reference view `inventory/products/index`
- Load the `frontend-design` skill for distinctive, production-grade interfaces within ADLMS constraints
- Design contracts in `docs/ui_*_design.md` follow Skill-Creator principles — honor their data contracts
- Never override branch isolation, permissions, or ledger rules for visual polish

## Skill-Creator Workflow

When authoring or extending agent skills for this project:

- Read the `create-skill` skill before writing `.cursor/skills/**/SKILL.md`
- Project skills live in `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` (never `~/.cursor/skills-cursor/`)
- Skills need YAML frontmatter (`name`, `description`) and trigger scenarios
- Keep skills focused: one workflow per skill; reference `docs/` rather than duplicating constitution text
- For modular monolith work, prefer `laravel-modular-monolith-architect` skill over ad-hoc scaffolding

## Laravel Modular Monolith Architect

Invoke when scaffolding modules, CRUD slices, workflow actions, or reviewing layering compliance.

## Pre-Commit Review Checklist

- Architecture: thin controllers, services own rules, repos own queries
- Branch: BranchContext used; no cross-branch leakage
- Inventory: ledger-derived; no mutable stock
- UI: design system, responsive, accessible, empty states
- Security: authorized routes, validated input, denial paths tested
- Tests: happy path + validation + auth + branch isolation (+ ledger for inventory)
